# Netlify: the files in the published folder that are not part of the site answer the not-found
# page. `404!` rather than `404`: a plain rule is shadowed by a file at the same path, and these
# are files that can be there: a build for no host in particular holds all three hosts'
# configurations and .nojekyll, and a plain `npx expo export` holds metadata.json. Netlify never
# serves _headers or _redirects itself; they are listed so the three configurations refuse the same
# paths. No rule names a repository file: Netlify reads this file only at the root of the folder
# it publishes, which holds none, and pointed at a checkout it finds no _redirects there at all.
# Cloudflare Pages ignores 404 rules: there, build with `--host cloudflare`, which leaves out
# .htaccess and .nojekyll, and `npm run build:web` leaves out metadata.json.
/_headers        /404.html  404!
/_redirects      /404.html  404!
/.htaccess       /404.html  404!
/.nojekyll       /404.html  404!
/metadata.json   /404.html  404!
